mercedes recently brought out a new  mid-range coupe sedan  the cla 200 is large and sporty like its  big brother the cls a four-door coupe  our test driver matas kurat took a  closer look at the cla 200.  mata says mercedes always calls the cla  a mid-range coupe sedan but it actually  builds on daimler's compact series the  a-class matas is going to see how well  it fits the mid-range category  the car's big grill has mean-looking  headlights and large air intakes  graceful lines flow together everywhere  underscoring the car's dynamism  nothing here seems out of place  the streamlined rear has a dual exhaust  and a well concealed rear view camera  but inside our tester finds one  incongruent detail  he likes the dashboard and all the  instruments the language of shape the  vents the materials used are all lovely  but the display in the middle of the  dash for the radio entertainment system  and navigation sticks out like a sore  thumb montes is sure this could have  been better integrated  the interior design is very reminiscent  of mercedes sls the steering wheel  speedometer and decorative elements all  have a sporty feel  the design is clearly structured except  for the myriad buttons on the curvy  central console  it's a luxurious ride up front but what  about the back seats  mata says the back seat shows that the  car is based on the a-class and the  coupe like roof line means the back  seats aren't comfortable for tall  passengers  at least there's lots of room for  luggage mata says the cla's 470 liter  trunk really is mid-range level it's  only five liters smaller than the  c-class  for more sportiness in the cla you can  spend an extra 2 000 euros for the speed  shift transmission  our test driver is pleased overall with  the cla  the cla's handling really pleases mantis  who says the car hugs the road and you  don't even notice that it's a  front-wheel drive that's because the  power steering reduces the typical  front-wheel drive  in our field  our test car's 115 kilowatts of power  accelerated to a maximum of 230  kilometers an hour its eco start stop  automatic optimizes fuel consumption and  city traffic  mata's current summary  mercedes has really done a good job of  avoiding confusing the cla and the  c-class the clas and c have smaller  engines those with the same names are  simply a bit less powerful except for  the c200cdi and the cla200cdi  which have the same push  the two series are geared to different  people the c-class is the sensible car  the more versatile one but also a little  more expensive the difference in price  is between two thousand and five  thousand euros depending on the engine  size the cla in contrast is more for the  lifestyle-oriented buyer who plans to  drive alone  affairs with an auto  our the urban variant of our test car  with a 7-speed automatic transmission  cost thirty seven thousand eight hundred  ninety euros in germany the basic model  is available for six thousand euros less  you
 

